From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 20:44:57 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] fix(control): alt+drag block-selects on a ghostty pane
 (KD-11)

Reported from use: block select works on a cascadia pane and does
nothing on a ghostty one - an alt+drag draws the ordinary linear
selection, with no error anywhere.

Both engines have the feature; they are told about it differently, and
the translation was missing. Cascadia is told once, at the click:
ControlCore::LeftClickOnTerminal takes altEnabled and calls
SetBlockSelection(altEnabled). GhosttyControlCore took the same
parameter and named it /*altEnabled*/.

ghostty asks per mouse event instead. SelectionGesture.drag takes a
`rectangle` flag, and Surface fills it in from the modifiers that came
with the latest mouse position, through SurfaceMouse:

    pub fn isRectangleSelectState(mods: input.Mods) bool {
        return if (comptime builtin.target.os.tag.isDarwin())
            mods.alt
        else
            mods.ctrlOrSuper() and mods.alt;
    }

Every mouse event the selection path sent carried GHOSTTY_MODS_NONE, so
the answer was always "no rectangle". Note the second branch: forwarding
WT's alt faithfully would not have been enough either - off macOS this
engine wants ctrl+alt.

So GhosttySelectionMods.h maps "WT says this drag is a block selection"
to the modifiers that predicate requires, and the core latches the alt
state at the click (as cascadia does - releasing alt mid-drag does not
turn a block selection back into a linear one) and puts those modifiers
on every mouse *position* of the drag.

Positions only. A press is read differently -
`if (mods.ctrlOrSuper()) .output else .line` chooses what a third click
selects - so a press claiming ctrl would quietly turn alt+triple-click
into "select the command's output". The presses stay bare.

Measured on the real engine, not reasoned: a new
GHOSTTY_HARNESS_SELECT_BLOCK drives this exact sequence over three rows
of distinct characters and reads the selection back. Dragging (2,0) to
(5,2) gives "CDE<LF>MNO<LF>WXY" with the modifiers and
"CDEFGHIJ<LF>KLMNOPQRST<LF>UVWXY" without, and the rectangle forms with
the press bare. smoke-harness pins both, and the contrast is the
regression signal - the bug was that the two were identical.

Suites: unitControl 63 -> 65/65, smoke 10 -> 11 checks.

Not covered: a double- or triple-click drag ignores the rectangle in
ghostty's gesture and in cascadia's expansion modes alike, so alt
changes nothing there on either engine; and ToggleBlockSelection - the
keyboard action that reshapes an existing selection - still returns
false, since the rectangle lives inside ghostty's Selection and no C
entry point reaches it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
